{
  "id": "LUK.24",
  "number": "24",
  "bookId": "LUK",
  "reference": "Luke 24",
  "copyright": "The Holy Bible, New International Version® NIV® Copyright © 1973, 1978, 1984, 2011 by Biblica, Inc.® Used by Permission of Biblica, Inc.® All rights reserved worldwide.",
  "verseCount": 53,
  "content": [
    {
      "name": "chapter",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "number": "24",
        "style": "c",
        "sid": "LUK 24"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "24",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "s1"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Jesus Has Risen",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "On the first day of the week, very early in the morning, the women took the spices they had prepared and went to the tomb.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "They found the stone rolled away from the tomb,",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "but when they entered, they did not find the body of the Lord Jesus.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "While they were wondering about this, suddenly two men in clothes that gleamed like lightning stood beside them.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In their fright the women bowed down with their faces to the ground, but the men said to them, \"Why do you look for the living among the dead?",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He is not here; he has risen! Remember how he told you, while he was still with you in Galilee:",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "char",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "wj"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "'The Son of Man must be delivered over to the hands of sinners, be crucified and on the third day be raised again.'",
              "type": "text",
              "attrs": {
                "verseId": "LUK.24.7",
                "verseOrgIds": [
                  "LUK.24.7"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "\"",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then they remembered his words.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.8"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "When they came back from the tomb, they told all these things to the Eleven and to all the others.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "It was Mary Magdalene, Joanna, Mary the mother of James, and the others with them who told this to the apostles.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But they did not believe the women, because their words seemed to them like nonsense.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Peter, however, got up and ran to the tomb. Bending over, he saw the strips of linen lying by themselves, and he went away, wondering to himself what had happened.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.12"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "s1"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "On the Road to Emmaus",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Now that same day two of them were going to a village called Emmaus, about seven miles",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "from Jerusalem.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "They were talking with each other about everything that had happened.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "As they talked and discussed these things with each other, Jesus himself came up and walked along with them;",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "but they were kept from recognizing him.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.16"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He asked them,",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.17"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "char",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "wj"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "\"What are you discussing together as you walk along?\"",
              "type": "text",
              "attrs": {
                "verseId": "LUK.24.17",
                "verseOrgIds": [
                  "LUK.24.17"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p",
        "vid": "LUK 24:17"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "They stood still, their faces downcast.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.17"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "18",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:18"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "18",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "One of them, named Cleopas, asked him, \"Are you the only one visiting Jerusalem who does not know the things that have happened there in these days?\"",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.18"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "19",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:19"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "19",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "char",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "wj"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "\"What things?\"",
              "type": "text",
              "attrs": {
                "verseId": "LUK.24.19",
                "verseOrgIds": [
                  "LUK.24.19"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "he asked.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.19"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p",
        "vid": "LUK 24:19"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "\"About Jesus of Nazareth,\" they replied. \"He was a prophet, powerful in word and deed before God and all the people.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.19"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "20",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:20"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "20",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The chief priests and our rulers handed him over to be sentenced to death, and they crucified him;",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.20",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.20"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "21",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:21"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "21",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "but we had hoped that he was the one who was going to redeem Israel. And what is more, it is the third day since all this took place.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.21"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "22",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:22"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "22",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In addition, some of our women amazed us. They went to the tomb early this morning",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.22",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.22"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "23",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:23"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "23",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "but didn't find his body. They came and told us that they had seen a vision of angels, who said he was alive.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.23"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "24",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:24"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "24",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then some of our companions went to the tomb and found it just as the women had said, but they did not see Jesus.\"",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.24",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.24"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "25",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:25"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "25",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He said to them,",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.25",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.25"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "char",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "wj"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "\"How foolish you are, and how slow to believe all that the prophets have spoken!",
              "type": "text",
              "attrs": {
                "verseId": "LUK.24.25",
                "verseOrgIds": [
                  "LUK.24.25"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.25",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.25"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "26",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:26"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "26",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "char",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "wj"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Did not the Messiah have to suffer these things and then enter his glory?\"",
              "type": "text",
              "attrs": {
                "verseId": "LUK.24.26",
                "verseOrgIds": [
                  "LUK.24.26"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.26",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.26"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "27",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:27"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "27",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And beginning with Moses and all the Prophets, he explained to them what was said in all the Scriptures concerning himself.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.27",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.27"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "28",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:28"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "28",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "As they approached the village to which they were going, Jesus continued on as if he were going farther.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.28",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.28"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "29",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:29"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "29",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But they urged him strongly, \"Stay with us, for it is nearly evening; the day is almost over.\" So he went in to stay with them.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.29",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.29"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "30",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:30"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "30",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "When he was at the table with them, he took bread, gave thanks, broke it and began to give it to them.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.30",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.30"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "31",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:31"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "31",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then their eyes were opened and they recognized him, and he disappeared from their sight.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.31",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.31"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "32",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:32"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "32",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "They asked each other, \"Were not our hearts burning within us while he talked with us on the road and opened the Scriptures to us?\"",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.32",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.32"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "33",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:33"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "33",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "They got up and returned at once to Jerusalem. There they found the Eleven and those with them, assembled together",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.33",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.33"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "34",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:34"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "34",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and saying, \"It is true! The Lord has risen and has appeared to Simon.\"",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.34",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.34"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "35",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:35"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "35",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then the two told what had happened on the way, and how Jesus was recognized by them when he broke the bread.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.35",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.35"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "s1"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Jesus Appears to the Disciples",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "36",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:36"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "36",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "While they were still talking about this, Jesus himself stood among them and said to them,",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.36",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.36"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "char",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "wj"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "\"Peace be with you.\"",
              "type": "text",
              "attrs": {
                "verseId": "LUK.24.36",
                "verseOrgIds": [
                  "LUK.24.36"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "37",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:37"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "37",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "They were startled and frightened, thinking they saw a ghost.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.37",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.37"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "38",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:38"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "38",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He said to them,",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.38",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.38"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "char",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "wj"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "\"Why are you troubled, and why do doubts rise in your minds?",
              "type": "text",
              "attrs": {
                "verseId": "LUK.24.38",
                "verseOrgIds": [
                  "LUK.24.38"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.38",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.38"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "39",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:39"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "39",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "char",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "wj"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Look at my hands and my feet. It is I myself! Touch me and see; a ghost does not have flesh and bones, as you see I have.\"",
              "type": "text",
              "attrs": {
                "verseId": "LUK.24.39",
                "verseOrgIds": [
                  "LUK.24.39"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "40",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:40"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "40",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "When he had said this, he showed them his hands and feet.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.40",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.40"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "41",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:41"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "41",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And while they still did not believe it because of joy and amazement, he asked them,",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.41",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.41"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "char",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "wj"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "\"Do you have anything here to eat?\"",
              "type": "text",
              "attrs": {
                "verseId": "LUK.24.41",
                "verseOrgIds": [
                  "LUK.24.41"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.41",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.41"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "42",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:42"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "42",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "They gave him a piece of broiled fish,",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.42",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.42"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "43",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:43"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "43",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and he took it and ate it in their presence.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.43",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.43"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "44",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:44"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "44",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He said to them,",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.44",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.44"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "char",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "wj"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "\"This is what I told you while I was still with you: Everything must be fulfilled that is written about me in the Law of Moses, the Prophets and the Psalms.\"",
              "type": "text",
              "attrs": {
                "verseId": "LUK.24.44",
                "verseOrgIds": [
                  "LUK.24.44"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "45",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:45"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "45",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then he opened their minds so they could understand the Scriptures.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.45",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.45"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "46",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:46"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "46",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He told them,",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.46",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.46"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "char",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "wj"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "\"This is what is written: The Messiah will suffer and rise from the dead on the third day,",
              "type": "text",
              "attrs": {
                "verseId": "LUK.24.46",
                "verseOrgIds": [
                  "LUK.24.46"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.46",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.46"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "47",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:47"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "47",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "char",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "wj"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "and repentance for the forgiveness of sins will be preached in his name to all nations, beginning at Jerusalem.",
              "type": "text",
              "attrs": {
                "verseId": "LUK.24.47",
                "verseOrgIds": [
                  "LUK.24.47"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.47",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.47"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "48",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:48"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "48",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "char",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "wj"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "You are witnesses of these things.",
              "type": "text",
              "attrs": {
                "verseId": "LUK.24.48",
                "verseOrgIds": [
                  "LUK.24.48"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.48",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.48"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "49",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:49"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "49",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "char",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "wj"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "I am going to send you what my Father has promised; but stay in the city until you have been clothed with power from on high.\"",
              "type": "text",
              "attrs": {
                "verseId": "LUK.24.49",
                "verseOrgIds": [
                  "LUK.24.49"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "s1"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "The Ascension of Jesus",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "50",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:50"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "50",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "When he had led them out to the vicinity of Bethany, he lifted up his hands and blessed them.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.50",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.50"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "51",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:51"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "51",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "While he was blessing them, he left them and was taken up into heaven.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.51",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.51"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "52",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:52"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "52",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then they worshiped him and returned to Jerusalem with great joy.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.52",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.52"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "53",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:53"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "53",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And they stayed continually at the temple, praising God.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.53",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.53"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "next": {
    "id": "JHN.intro",
    "number": "intro",
    "bookId": "JHN"
  },
